---
description: Use agent-skills workflows from .cursor/skills
alwaysApply: true
---

Before non-trivial technical work:

1. Route via `.cursor/skills/using-agent-skills/SKILL.md`.
2. Read and follow the matching skill under `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.
3. Open `reference.md` in that folder when the skill links to it. Shared checklists live in `.cursor/references/`.
4. Prefer project skills over guessing; user does not need to say "read skill" each time.

Lifecycle slash commands (type `/` in chat) map to skills of the same name:

- `/spec` → spec-driven-development
- `/plan` → planning-and-task-breakdown
- `/build` (and `/build auto`) → incremental-implementation + test-driven-development
- `/test` → test-driven-development
- `/review` → code-review-and-quality
- `/webperf` → performance-optimization via web-performance-auditor
- `/code-simplify` → code-simplification
- `/ship` → shipping-and-launch
